== The Research Foundation

#block(
  fill: rgb("#e8f5e9"),
  stroke: 2pt,
  radius: 4pt,
  inset: 14pt,
  width: 100%,
)[
  #text(weight: "bold", size: 12pt)[Scaling Quantum Teleportation: The Scientific Foundation]
  #v(10pt)
  #text(size: 11pt)[
    The founding team's vision to scale quantum teleportation from mini to macro was grounded in a comprehensive review of the latest quantum teleportation research. By January 2026, the scientific literature had demonstrated remarkable progress:
    
    #v(10pt)
    
    #text(weight: "bold")[Key Research Findings:]
    
    #v(6pt)
    
    • #text(weight: "bold")[Deterministic teleportation between distant superconducting chips] (64-meter distances) - proving that quantum teleportation could work over macroscopic distances between separate quantum processors
    
    • #text(weight: "bold")[Teleportation coexisting with classical communications] (30.2 km fiber links) - demonstrating that quantum and classical signals could share the same infrastructure
    
    • #text(weight: "bold")[Thermal microwave network teleportation] (up to 4K temperatures) - showing resilience to thermal noise and the potential for practical deployment
    
    • #text(weight: "bold")[Black hole simulation teleportation] - revealing connections between quantum teleportation and fundamental physics
    
    #v(10pt)
    
    These papers, compiled in the *Quantum Teleportation Research Foundation* booklet, provided the theoretical and experimental foundation for Teleport Massive's mission. The research showed a clear trajectory: teleportation was scaling up—from particles to chips, from short distances to kilometers, from ideal conditions to real-world environments.
    
    #v(10pt)
    
    The founding team recognized that if teleportation could work between distant chips, it could potentially work for larger objects. If it could coexist with classical signals, it could be deployed in existing infrastructure. If it could operate at higher temperatures, it could be more practical. Their mission was to systematically push these boundaries: to teleport bigger and bigger things safely, making distance irrelevant for all of humanity.
  ]
]

